 "cues": [
  {
   "s": 0.6,
   "e": 4.02,
   "text": "Say you ask an AI agent to swap 500 USDC."
  },
  {
   "s": 4.06,
   "e": 5.32,
   "text": "That request is an intent."
  },
  {
   "s": 5.36,
   "e": 7.34,
   "text": "Before it can safely settle onchain,"
  },
  {
   "s": 7.38,
   "e": 10.301,
   "text": "it has to pass three security gates in our system."
  },
  {
   "s": 10.341,
   "e": 11.863,
   "text": "Let's walk through them."
  },
  {
   "s": 12.913,
   "e": 15.938,
   "text": "First, the model doesn't touch the chain directly."
  },
  {
   "s": 15.978,
   "e": 18.62,
   "text": "It works inside an execution harness."
  },
  {
   "s": 18.66,
   "e": 20.628,
   "text": "The model makes one typed call,"
  },
  {
   "s": 20.668,
   "e": 22.149,
   "text": "and the harness does the rest:"
  },
  {
   "s": 22.189,
   "e": 25.041,
   "text": "it reads chain state, stages the transaction,"
  },
  {
   "s": 25.081,
   "e": 27.381,
   "text": "simulates it, and commits it."
  },
  {
   "s": 28.281,
   "e": 30.006,
   "text": "Why do we need gates at all?"
  },
  {
   "s": 30.046,
   "e": 33.57,
   "text": "A financial agent works a lot like a coding agent:"
  },
  {
   "s": 33.61,
   "e": 36.658,
   "text": "it takes an intent, builds something, and ships it."
  },
  {
   "s": 36.698,
   "e": 39.584,
   "text": "But code is reviewed and tested before it deploys,"
  },
  {
   "s": 39.624,
   "e": 42.196,
   "text": "while a transaction is only signed."
  },
  {
   "s": 42.236,
   "e": 45.83,
   "text": "Along the way it can be attacked, or simply built wrong."
  },
  {
   "s": 45.87,
   "e": 48.071,
   "text": "And once it settles, it's final,"
  },
  {
   "s": 48.111,
   "e": 52.037,
   "text": "even when it's valid onchain but wrong for the user."
  },
  {
   "s": 56.087,
   "e": 58.624,
   "text": "At the build step, we simulate the transaction"
  },
  {
   "s": 58.664,
   "e": 61.794,
   "text": "against a fork of the live chain, again and again."
  },
  {
   "s": 61.834,
   "e": 64.987,
   "text": "When a simulation fails, the error goes back to the model,"
  },
  {
   "s": 65.027,
   "e": 67.935,
   "text": "which fixes the transaction and tries again."
  },
  {
   "s": 67.975,
   "e": 70.315,
   "text": "Only a transaction that passes is committed."
  },
  {
   "s": 70.355,
   "e": 73.88,
   "text": "We call this gate 0.5, because it runs inside the harness,"
  },
  {
   "s": 73.92,
   "e": 76.313,
   "text": "while the agent is still building."
  },
  {
   "s": 79.564,
   "e": 81.567,
   "text": "Once the agent has built the transaction,"
  },
  {
   "s": 81.607,
   "e": 85.248,
   "text": "it still can't sign it, because it never holds the key."
  },
  {
   "s": 85.288,
   "e": 87.872,
   "text": "Instead, it sends a signing request to a separate"
  },
  {
   "s": 87.912,
   "e": 90.798,
   "text": "wallet module running in a secure enclave."
  },
  {
   "s": 90.838,
   "e": 94.048,
   "text": "That module checks the request against the user's policy,"
  },
  {
   "s": 94.088,
   "e": 95.163,
   "text": "such as spending limits,"
  },
  {
   "s": 95.203,
   "e": 98.716,
   "text": "allowed contracts and recipients, and only then signs."
  },
  {
   "s": 98.756,
   "e": 100.255,
   "text": "This is gate one."
  },
  {
   "s": 102.605,
   "e": 104.643,
   "text": "Gate two runs onchain."
  },
  {
   "s": 104.683,
   "e": 107.244,
   "text": "A guard contract on the user's account checks"
  },
  {
   "s": 107.284,
   "e": 110.646,
   "text": "every transaction against rules the user has set,"
  },
  {
   "s": 110.686,
   "e": 113.943,
   "text": "like a sanctions blocklist or a spending cap."
  },
  {
   "s": 113.983,
   "e": 117.46,
   "text": "If a transaction breaks a rule, the contract reverts it,"
  },
  {
   "s": 117.5,
   "e": 119.627,
   "text": "even if the signer approved it."
  },
  {
   "s": 120.477,
   "e": 123.131,
   "text": "Finally, the signed transaction waits in the"
  },
  {
   "s": 123.171,
   "e": 126.11,
   "text": "mempool until a block builder picks it up."
  },
  {
   "s": 126.363,
   "e": 128.169,
   "text": "As the builder packs the block,"
  },
  {
   "s": 128.209,
   "e": 130.085,
   "text": "it checks each transaction against"
  },
  {
   "s": 130.125,
   "e": 131.768,
   "text": "the protocol's assertions."
  },
  {
   "s": 131.808,
   "e": 132.709,
   "text": "If one fails,"
  },
  {
   "s": 132.749,
   "e": 135.426,
   "text": "the builder removes it before the block is sealed."
  },
  {
   "s": 135.466,
   "e": 137.406,
   "text": "This is the last gate."
  },
  {
   "s": 138.056,
   "e": 139.966,
   "text": "Only then is the block added to the chain,"
  },
  {
   "s": 140.006,
   "e": 142.168,
   "text": "and the transaction is settled."
  },
  {
   "s": 143.618,
   "e": 145.157,
   "text": "Each gate sees something different,"
  },
  {
   "s": 145.197,
   "e": 147.776,
   "text": "so no single gate can catch everything."
  },
  {
   "s": 148.626,
   "e": 150.629,
   "text": "Put together, every risk is stopped"
  },
  {
   "s": 150.669,
   "e": 152.441,
   "text": "at the checkpoint that can see it."
  },
  {
   "s": 152.481,
   "e": 156.016,
   "text": "Simulation catches wrong decimals and stale routes."
  },
  {
   "s": 156.056,
   "e": 158.733,
   "text": "The signing policy catches a swapped payload,"
  },
  {
   "s": 158.773,
   "e": 160.916,
   "text": "and partly a forged instruction."
  },
  {
   "s": 160.956,
   "e": 163.505,
   "text": "The onchain guard blocks a policy breach,"
  },
  {
   "s": 163.545,
   "e": 165.224,
   "text": "like a sanctioned recipient."
  },
  {
   "s": 165.264,
   "e": 167.685,
   "text": "And the builder drops a sandwich attack."
  },
  {
   "s": 167.725,
   "e": 171.221,
   "text": "Only a transaction that passes every gate settles."
  },
  {
   "s": 172.471,
   "e": 175.241,
   "text": "This idea goes beyond our own implementation."
  },
  {
   "s": 175.281,
   "e": 177.837,
   "text": "It applies to any financial workflow."
  },
  {
   "s": 178.337,
   "e": 181.478,
   "text": "The human's identity is canonical and persistent;"
  },
  {
   "s": 181.518,
   "e": 183.765,
   "text": "it's the account that holds the real money."
  },
  {
   "s": 183.805,
   "e": 186.029,
   "text": "From it, the user authorizes sessions,"
  },
  {
   "s": 186.069,
   "e": 189.593,
   "text": "which let agents act only on approved resources."
  },
  {
   "s": 189.633,
   "e": 193.1,
   "text": "Each session's authority is scoped, capped, and expires."
  },
  {
   "s": 193.14,
   "e": 194.876,
   "text": "The same checks work onchain,"
  },
  {
   "s": 194.916,
   "e": 197.512,
   "text": "at a bank, or on an exchange."
  },
  {
   "s": 197.552,
   "e": 200.421,
   "text": "You can think of it as OAuth for money."
  },
  {
   "s": 203.371,
   "e": 205.142,
   "text": "That's how Aomi takes an agent's"
  },
  {
   "s": 205.182,
   "e": 207.244,
   "text": "transaction from intent to settlement."
  },
  {
   "s": 207.284,
   "e": 210.641,
   "text": "You can read the full research at aomi.dev."
  }
 ],
